 17592186045417] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186054809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1031 "The Cartesian Coordinate System" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1033 92 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1034 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186050517 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "50123c1c-7113-541e-8c4f-047f2eec416d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096509 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5343" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096509 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola shown below?\n\n![](images/52/527ab20a54cc8191b5ef618d99601e77ca2ef4e757ee5f83ddf4c868bf0e5b15.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096509 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31dd152b-cab9-5754-9335-42ed830d3c01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096509 #edb/ref 1074 "The vertex of a right-opening parabola is the left-most point of the parabola.\n\n![](images/bf/bfb2b1ce3cccea8a22732a061dd8ace5ad1b3c808feb5c1ec074802f7daf4d1a.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(-4,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096566 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7472" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096566 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the vertex of the parabola shown below?\n\n![](images/41/4183a3f0f864d0bda19d9b4c42d69952af51423fb1024d311b6a863e8e4ee037.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096566 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "34e8e4aa-b8c8-518d-857a-42ac8f7345b9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096566 #edb/ref 1074 "The vertex of a downward-opening parabola is the highest point of the parabola.\n\n![](images/fb/fb7fa7a4dcc4c7746122cd01a79a03584eb74c2ce9439859910699278e971a56.png)\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the vertex are $(4,3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096567 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096567 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(x+1)^2=8(y-2)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096567 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "40e08a6f-a312-5f00-8b4a-e5fe8fe3cefb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096567 #edb/ref 1074 "The standard equation of an upward- or downward-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-h)^2 = 4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)^{2} & =4(2)(y-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p =2.$\n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h= -1$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $(-1,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096568 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096568 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola $(y-2)^2=2(x+1)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096568 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "258f64db-05c1-5314-a6d8-aa2f604f5c95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096568 #edb/ref 1074 "The standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(h,k)$ is\n\n$$\n(y-k)^2 = 4p(x-h),\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is a constant.\n\nWe can rewrite the given equation as \n\n$$\n(y-2)^2 = 4\\left(\\dfrac{2}{4}\\right)(x +1),\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies to\n\n$$\n(y-2)^2 = 4\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)(x +1),\n$$\n\nIt is now clear that our equation is of the standard type with $p=\\dfrac{1}{2}.$ \n\nComparing our equation with the standard equation, we can see that we have $h=-1$ and $k=2.$ Therefore, the coordinates of the vertex of the parabola are $\\left(-1,2\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250503 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253483 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354362 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354364 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186354365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375762 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186377941 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394599 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186440818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying the Vertex of a Horizontal Parabola Given Its Graph" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096711 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "61861939-69d4-5b1e-a0f0-6a1b383b775b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186097016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250500 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186250502 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186253509 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186375748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186377934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096761 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186386889 #e